{"chunk_id": "ec6fae44ab03", "text": "Yudhishthira approves Kunti\u2019s compassionate decision to help the afflicted Brahmana whose family was doomed to feed the man\u2011eating Rakshasa Vaka. Bhima secretly carries the food meant for the monster and deliberately provokes him by eating it himself. When the enraged Rakshasa attacks, Bhima ignores the blows until he finishes the meal, then calmly rises to fight. The two hurl uprooted trees and grapple with immense force, shaking the earth. Bhima eventually overpowers Vaka, breaks his body across his knee, and kills him. He warns the other Rakshasas to abandon cannibalism, leaves Vaka\u2019s corpse at the town gate, and returns unseen. The townspeople later discover the body and marvel at the unknown hero, while the Brahmana conceals the Pandavas\u2019 involvement. The episode highlights Bhima\u2019s strength and the Pandavas\u2019 hidden heroism while protecting the innocent.\nBhima confronts the cannibal Vaka, taunts him by eating his food, and defeats the monster in a brutal wrestling fight.\nThemes: heroic combat, monster slaying, protection of townspeople, physical strength", "vector": [0.008189275860786438, -0.03625725209712982, 0.0012507683131843805, 0.019691668450832367, -0.013018677942454815, 0.026331260800361633, -0.026678603142499924, -0.023459002375602722, -0.018769873306155205, -0.03382585197687149, 0.011074893176555634, -0.007935448549687862, 0.008924040012061596, -0.02518235705792904, -0.011108292266726494, 0.005490689072757959, 0.05079221352934837, -0.010433644987642765, 0.015737304463982582, -0.020279480144381523, 0.002045649103820324, 0.0013083803933113813, 0.01240414846688509, 0.02061346359550953, -0.033211320638656616, 0.02260400541126728, 0.026170948520302773, -0.021428382024168968, 0.011368799023330212, -0.014361291192471981, 0.008236033841967583, -0.015817459672689438, -0.006699709687381983, 0.0038508300203830004, -0.019878698512911797, 0.0008708620443940163, -0.0018920166185125709, -0.029123364